      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-15326",
      ":question/problem": "A software house estimates that its revenue, in thousands of dollars, is given by\n$R(x) =-x^{2} + 64x + 25$,\nwhere $x$ is the number of projects taken on in a particular year. The company has the capacity to take on $50$ projects per year at most. How many projects should the software house take on each year to maximize its revenue?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
