      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-51329",
      ":question/problem": "The foreman estimates that the profit of his factory, in thousands of dollars, is given by\n$P(x) =-x^{2} + 12x - 2$,\nwhere $x$ is the number of items, in hundreds, produced daily. Given that the factory can produce at most $1000$ items per day, how many items should the factory produce per day to maximize its daily profit?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
